From 286236ba1d25ffaca3a4996c4b7adc9c1bb4e016 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Oleg Tolmatcev <oleg.tolmatcev@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 12:20:18 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 21/21] feat(windows): replace libtool's MSYS path conversion

With build and host both MinGW, libtool assumes the shell is MSYS and
converts paths with `cmd //c echo PATH`, relying on MSYS to turn `//c`
into `/c`.  A native shell passes `//c` through unchanged; cmd.exe does
not take it as a switch and starts an interactive session, so linking
a DLL hangs or links against cmd.exe's banner.

Replace the conversion with the same sed transformation, minus cmd: the
paths are Windows paths already.  libtool 2.4 to 2.4.2 converts inline
in func_to_host_path and func_to_host_pathlist (a generated copy of the
latter differs by an article in a diagnostic); 2.4.3 and later call
func_convert_core_msys_to_w32, whose 2.6 version also handles the
original MSYS's `cmd /c`.

Assisted-by: Claude Code:claude-opus-5-5
